<%# The tint alone would say it to the eye only, which RGAA 3.1 refuses. The
    wording is read once, off screen, and after the value rather than before: a
    heading otherwise announces the mark and then what it marks. It joins the
    value with no space between them, the comma being part of the sentence, and
    rides the tooltip for whoever hovers it. %>
<%= tag.span(class: 'directory-value', lang:, title: label) do %><%= content %><span class="fr-sr-only"><%= meaning %></span><% end %>
